102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (You can create various types of Seaborn plots by using different functions provided by the Seaborn library, such as sns.scatterplot\(\) for scatter plots, sns.barplot\(\) for bar plots, sns.boxplot\(\) for box plots, sns.histplot\(\) for histograms, sns.lineplot\(\) for line plots, and so on. Each function is tailored to create a specific type of plot, allowing you to visualize your data in different ways.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 66 0 R
/T (6. How can I customise Seaborn plots with titles, labels, and legends?)
/E (6. How can I customise Seaborn plots with titles, labels, and legends?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (In Matplotlib, customizing plots involves a few straightforward steps. First, import the library using import matplotlib.pyplot as plt. Then, create your plot with plt.plot\(x, y, label='Line 1'\). To add a title, use plt.title\('Sample Plot'\), and to label the axes, use plt.xlabel\('X Axis Label'\) and plt.ylabel\('Y Axis Label'\). Add a legend with plt.legend\(\). Finally, display the plot using plt.show\(\). These steps ensure your plot is informative and well-labeled.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
