/P 67 0 R
/E (To create a PairGrid in Python using Seaborn, you use the seaborn.PairGrid\(\) function. PairGrid is useful for exploring relationships between multiple variables in a dataset by creating a grid of subplots, where each subplot shows the relationship between a pair of variables. It's particularly handy for visualizing correlations and distributions in multivariate data.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
